    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Experimental design",
    "reading_order" : 9,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 3,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000010",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "The concentrations of the other reactants, propanone and H<sup>+</sup>, do not change",
    "reading_order" : 10,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000011",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "A **large excess** of both propanone and the acid catalyst is used",
    "reading_order" : 11,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000012",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "This means that their concentrations will remain effectively constant throughout the experiment",
    "reading_order" : 12,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000013",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Method (sampling and quenching)",
    "reading_order" : 13,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "heading",
    "heading_level" : 3,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000014",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "We need to find the concentration of iodine at various points in time, so we use a sampling and titration method",
    "reading_order" : 14,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000015",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "1. Mix 25 cm<sup>3</sup> of 1.0 mol dm<sup>-3 </sup>aqueous propanone with 25 cm<sup>3</sup> of 1.0 mol dm<sup>-3</sup> sulfuric acid in a beaker\n2. Add 50 cm<sup>3</sup> of 0.02 mol dm<sup>-3</sup> iodine solution",
    "reading_order" : 15,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000016",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**Start the timer as soon this is added to the beaker**",
    "reading_order" : 16,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000017",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "3. At regular intervals, use a pipette to withdraw 10 cm<sup>3</sup> portion of the reaction mixture and transfer this to a conical flask\n4. **Quench **/ stop the sample reacting further by adding a spatula of sodium hydrogen carbonate\n5. Titrate the sample against 0.01 mol dm<sup>-3 </sup>sodium thiosulfate(VI) solution using starch as an indicator",
    "reading_order" : 17,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000018",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "Starch is used as an indicator is used to determine the concentration of iodine",
    "reading_order" : 18,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "list_item",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000019",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "**2S**<sub>**2**</sub>**O**<sub>**3**</sub><sup>**2-**</sup>** (aq) + I**<sub>**2**</sub>** (aq) → 2I**<sup>**-**</sup>** (aq) + S**<sub>**4**</sub>**O**<sub>**6**</sub><sup>**2- **</sup>**(aq) **",
    "reading_order" : 19,
    "confidence" : 1.0,
    "role" : "paragraph",
    "heading_level" : null,
    "source_engine" : "sme-revision-note",
    "source_engine_version" : "1.0.0"
  }, {
    "element_id" : "e000020",
    "element_type" : "text_block",
    "page_number" : 1,
    "bounding_box" : null,
    "text" : "6. Record the result for each titration in a suitable table",
    "reading_order" : 20,
